## Decisions and Action Items

* **Decisions**:
  * The WG will target Last Call for the core draft (`draft-ietf-ocm-open-cloud-mesh`) around December 2026.
  * The array batching proposal will be put on hold and not pursued for the core draft.
* **Action Items**:
  * **Micke Nordin** to submit a Pull Request introducing `collection_id` into the core specification.
  * **Giuseppe Presti** to update the Distributed Directory Service PR, resolving issues regarding the "share type" misnomer and removing the unnecessary JSON endpoint.
  * **WG Chairs (Thibault Meunier / Lisa)** to request an early review of the HTTP directory and message signature components of `draft-ietf-ocm-open-cloud-mesh` from the IETF HTTP Directorate.
  * **WG Chairs** to coordinate the logistical setup for the hybrid IETF 128 / CS3 session.

---

## Next Steps

* **Milestone Updates**: The WG will look into extending the milestones for the newly adopted companion drafts (`draft-ietf-ocm-integration-protocol` and `draft-ietf-ocm-mls-federated-groups`) into 2027 to allow the core specification to finalize first.
* **Mailing List Discussion**: Further refinement of the distributed directory service design and its placement (within the core draft versus the MLS draft) will be conducted on the OCM mailing list.